pastex (1.10.7-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Bring the window back after the paste. Muffin reported wm state "normal"
    for a window it had left minimized, so the restore loop believed it was
    visible after one deiconify() that the window manager had dropped during
    the minimize animation, and Pastex stayed minimized. The request is now
    repeated every 60 ms for at least 400 ms whatever the state says (and for
    up to 1.2 s while it still reports iconic), after 240 ms the window
    manager is asked to activate the window with xdotool windowactivate
    --sync, and the log states when the window was restored.
  * Claim the clipboard in Tk before reading it back. Reading first cost
    about a second per click on a machine where both clipboard readers are
    slow (each read waits for its timeout), which made the text appear late.
    Tk owning the selection is instant and cannot be lost, so it is done
    first and the single read after it only decides between Ctrl+V and the
    typed delivery. The focus check also starts at 120 ms instead of 200 ms.
  * Log how long the clipboard check and the typing took, so a slow click can
    be read from the log instead of guessed at.

