pastex (1.10.6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Type the snippet when the clipboard cannot hold it. On the reporting
    machine xclip reports success, the clipboard reads back empty even after
    Tk claims the selection, and 1.10.5 therefore cancelled the paste. The
    text now arrives anyway: when the clipboard cannot be made to hold it,
    Pastex types the snippet into the target window with xdotool (through a
    temporary file, so a snippet that starts with "-" is not read as an
    option) instead of pressing Ctrl+V on an empty clipboard. The text is
    delivered exactly once either way, and only a text longer than 20 000
    characters stops the paste and says so.
  * Believe only a non-empty clipboard read. A single broken reader used to
    make a full clipboard look empty and cancel a paste that would have
    worked; xclip, xsel and wl-paste are all consulted now and an empty answer
    is accepted only when every reader agrees.
  * pastex --check explains the empty read-back and the typed delivery.

