pastex (1.10.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Never leave the window minimized, and stop skipping Ctrl+V on a slow
    minimize. The hide check gave up after 300 ms, but Cinnamon animates the
    minimize for a few hundred milliseconds; when the window finished hiding
    just after the check, Pastex had already decided "never hidden", sent no
    Ctrl+V and left the window minimized. The check now allows 600 ms.
  * Restore the window instead of giving up on it. The branch that concluded
    "the window never hid" did not deiconify anything, so a minimize that
    completed a moment later was permanent. It now asks for the window back
    and logs the observed state.
  * Verify the restore. deiconify() is dropped when it arrives while the
    minimize animation is still running, which also left the window minimized
    for good. The state is now re-read every 60 ms for up to 1.2 s and the
    request is repeated until the window is really back, in every path
    (success, failure, watchdog deadline and the give-up case).
  * Do not overwrite a running paste with the manual hint. When the <Unmap>
    signal released Ctrl+V before the copy worker reported back, the copy
    result replaced the status with "press Ctrl+V" even though the sender was
    already running; a _paste_started flag keeps that path quiet.
  * Seven new tests and three new mutation checks cover the restore path.

